    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 14.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="14.1" corresp="#wit-hk">E ki blasmé unt esté se escundirunt par serment numé, ceo est a saver par XIIII humes leals par num; s'il les pot aver si s'en escundira sei duzime main.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk">And those who have been (previously) accused shall clear themselves by the oath with selected compurgators, that is by means of 14 qualified men nominated [by the court], of whom 11 must act as the accused man's compurgators to clear him of the charge, if he can find as many to do so.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="503"><ref target="clause:IICn_65">II Cn 65</ref>; <ref target="clause:LeisWl_15">Leis Wl 15</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. ebd. 65 u. 15</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_15">Leis Wl 15</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 260–261 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
    </body>
